{
  "caseId": "averitec-dev-0058",
  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "atom-1",
      "text": "Russia sent medical aid to the US.",
      "sourceText": "Russia sent medical aid to the US, in the form of medical equipment to help coronavirus patients.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 97
    },
    {
      "id": "atom-2",
      "text": "The aid was in the form of medical equipment.",
      "sourceText": "Russia sent medical aid to the US, in the form of medical equipment to help coronavirus patients.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 97
    },
    {
      "id": "atom-3",
      "text": "The aid was sent to help coronavirus patients.",
      "sourceText": "Russia sent medical aid to the US, in the form of medical equipment to help coronavirus patients.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 97
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "atomId": "atom-1",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "Turning the Tables, Russia Sends Virus Aid to U.S.\n",
          "start": 27,
          "end": 78
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-16",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "The US sent $5.6 million in medical supplies to Russia to help it combat the coronavirus pandemic. ",
          "start": 2405,
          "end": 2504
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-15",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "Democrats were also outraged over the difference in the cost and amount of medical aid provided by Russia to the US versus that delivered by the US to Russia.\n",
          "start": 2246,
          "end": 2405
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-19",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "Speaking alongside members of his coronavirus task force in the White House Rose Garden on March 30, Trump said, “Russia sent us a very, very large planeload of things, medical equipment, which was very nice.”\n",
          "start": 2848,
          "end": 3058
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-63",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "The government-backed Russian Direct Investment Fund, which paid for half the shipment, said it was working with U.S. companies to deliver medical supplies to Russia if they are needed.\n",
          "start": 8919,
          "end": 9105
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-10",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "After plans for the shipment stirred criticism on both sides of the Atlantic, the Foreign Ministry in Moscow said on Thursday that the two countries had in fact evenly split the cost of the medical goods and that Russia could depend on future aid from the United States in fighting the coronavirus.\n",
          "start": 1152,
          "end": 1451
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-16",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "The US sent $5.6 million in medical supplies to Russia to help it combat the coronavirus pandemic. ",
          "start": 2405,
          "end": 2504
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "Turning the Tables, Russia Sends Virus Aid to U.S.\n",
          "start": 27,
          "end": 78
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-17",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "A video posted to the Twitter account of the US Embassy in Moscow in June showed an American military cargo plane arriving with some of the aid, including 200 ventilators.\n",
          "start": 2504,
          "end": 2676
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-45",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "- Hospitals and medical centers. ",
          "start": 6212,
          "end": 6245
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-63",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "The government-backed Russian Direct Investment Fund, which paid for half the shipment, said it was working with U.S. companies to deliver medical supplies to Russia if they are needed.\n",
          "start": 8919,
          "end": 9105
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-15",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "Democrats were also outraged over the difference in the cost and amount of medical aid provided by Russia to the US versus that delivered by the US to Russia.\n",
          "start": 2246,
          "end": 2405
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-16",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "The US sent $5.6 million in medical supplies to Russia to help it combat the coronavirus pandemic. ",
          "start": 2405,
          "end": 2504
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "A planeload of coronavirus aid to New York was a propaganda coup for the Kremlin — tempered by an intensifying epidemic at home.\n",
          "start": 78,
          "end": 207
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "Turning the Tables, Russia Sends Virus Aid to U.S.\n",
          "start": 27,
          "end": 78
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-bacc7d0e399e::sentence-32",
          "documentId": "doc-bacc7d0e399e",
          "text": "On Aug. 23, the Food and Drug Administration granted full approval to Pfizer-BioNTech’s coronavirus vaccine for people 16 and up, paving the way for an increase in mandates in both the public and private sectors. ",
          "start": 4864,
          "end": 5077
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-1",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "As the US was bracing for a major wave of seriously ill coronavirus patients in March, President Donald Trump asked President Vladimir Putin in a phone call for help. ",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 167
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ff8f3576e3da::sentence-19",
          "documentId": "doc-ff8f3576e3da",
          "text": "Speaking alongside members of his coronavirus task force in the White House Rose Garden on March 30, Trump said, “Russia sent us a very, very large planeload of things, medical equipment, which was very nice.”\n",
          "start": 2848,
          "end": 3058
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
